<title>USA: El Salvador seeks 8,000-10,000 T U.S. soymeal.</title>
<headline>El Salvador seeks 8,000-10,000 T U.S. soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>El Salvador was tendering for about 8,000 to 10,000 tonnes of U.S. soybean meal in bulk under the PL-480, Title I export program, its shipping agent, International Services Corp, said.</p>
<p>The soybean meal, 48 percent minimum, minimum 0.5 percent crude fat, maximum 3.5 percent crude fiber, maximum 12.0 moisture, was slated for April 21-May 6 delivery.</p>
<p>Offers are to be received by April 14 and will remain valid on April 15.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
</text>
